Description: spiDE identifies context-specific, neighbourhood-dependent
    differential expression in spatial transcriptomics data. Within an index
    cell type, it tests how gene expression changes with an experimental
    condition as a function of the local density (niche) of surrounding cell
    types. Niche covariates are constructed from Gaussian kernel density
    estimates at multiple bandwidths; a per-gene negative binomial GLM is fit
    using the SpaNorm fitting engine; and neighbourhood effects are tested via
    Wald statistics combined across correlated covariates (Cauchy combination by
    default, or Brown's method), across bandwidths (Cauchy combination), and
    corrected with a hierarchical false discovery rate procedure.
